   "circularity: the positives are E1's outputs on the fetched subsets and C_rules encodes E1's minted-return shape at IL level (ret preceded by newobj), so recall@k partly measures agreement with E1's criterion; the logistic model's top weights say the same (ret<-newobj +0.76, has_body +0.75, tok_Decode +0.68; has_disposable_param -0.87, calls_pinvoke -0.51)",
   "B (LLM) lists were capped at 15 per library by the discovery protocol, so B's recall@25 is bounded by list length; the fair comparison with B is at k = 10",
   "the arms' queues admit interface members and property getters; E1 cannot prove bodiless members and getters are aliases, so A's and C's queues wasted executions there (A: 5 of 10, C: 4 of 10); an 'exclude getters and bodiless members' rule is the obvious refinement and was NOT applied post hoc"
  ]
