 "gates": {
  "KILL CT-1 (C not better than A and B on validated novel rows per validator execution)": "NOT TRIGGERED: C_lr 3 PROVED of 10 executions; A 0 of 10; B (LLM unproven candidates) 0 of 10; on the recall proxy C_rules/C_lr pooled recall@10 0.588 vs B 0.553 vs A 0.401 and recall@25 0.813/0.779 vs 0.685 vs 0.595",
  "KILL CT-2 (C only re-discovers what E1/E2/E3 derive)": "NOT TRIGGERED on the letter: 3 NOVEL BODY_PROVED rows (Org.BouncyCastle.Cms.CmsCompressedDataStreamGenerator.Open, MQTTnet.Certificates.BlobCertificateProvider.GetCertificate, Npgsql.Internal.NpgsqlConnector.CreateCommand). CAVEAT that narrows the hypothesis: all three were proved by E1 itself once pointed at their source file; 'novel' means beyond the 25-file subset E1 had seen, not a shape E1 cannot derive; a whole-repository derivation would find them without any ranker",
  "KILL CT-3 (cross-version predictions systematically refuted)": "NOT TRIGGERED: 32 of 32 exact-binary witnesses fresh (SKBitmap.Decode, SKBitmap.FromImage, SKData.AsStream, SKFont.GetTextPath on 3.119.4, 4.148.0, 4.152.0, 4.153.1; net6.0 and netstandard2.0 assets); moreover version portability is settled by identity, not prediction: the normalised IL-body hash of all 28 overloads is identical across the 8 assets while it discriminates 429 changed methods between 3.119.4 and 4.153.1",
  "KILL CT-4 (signal only with hundreds/thousands of labels)": "NOT TRIGGERED: Gate 0 used the 131 existing positives and the LLM negatives; no labelling campaign",
  "pass_shape (C beats A and B per 100 candidates; >= 3 NOVEL rows; >= 1 portability recovery)": "MET ON THE LETTER (30 vs 0 vs 0 per 100; 3 novel; 12 portability recoveries by witness) but NOT in spirit: the recoveries came from the witness and the IL-hash identity, and the novel rows from E1 over files it had not been given; nothing here requires a learned model"
 },
 "decisions": {
  "H-21 relational candidate discovery": "NARROW + KEEP_AS_CANDIDATE_GENERATOR: the cheap relational ranker (C) is kept as the queue for the runtime witness on binary-only surfaces and for the non-provable remainder (lock bodies, target-typed new, ambient tokens); learned walks (CodeTrek-like) NOT ADVANCED: no demanding instance remains once (a) the body proof runs over the whole source tree instead of a 25-file subset and (b) rows are pinned by the IL-body hash; CT-4 also forbids the labels a learned model would need",
  "H-09 identity granularity": "KEEP_AS_VALIDATOR, sharpened: row identity = (assembly simple name, callable signature, normalised IL-body hash); the MVID stays the per-file identity for the load-chain check; the ref/lib NARROW and the v2 'MVID per TFM' multiplicity are resolved by the per-row hash (0 of 28 row overloads differ across 8 assets; 15 of 1926 methods differ between the net6.0 and netstandard2.0 assets of one version, all TFM-conditional code)",
  "H-20": "confirmed as the cause of the v2 portability gap: the v2 re-derivation ran without the throw-exit seam and lost exactly the guarded factories",
  "H-04 / H-11": "unchanged; the census shows the LLM arm's 'undecidable' candidates include the most used factories of three libraries, so the witness queue for them is worth more than any further proof effort"
 },
 "recommended_next_experiment": {
  "title": "CT-breadth then density: whole-source-tree derivation pinned by IL-body hash, then a consumer run on the census-dense repositories with one exposure base",
  "steps": [
   "derive BODY_PROVED rows over the ENTIRE source tree of each of the 22 libraries at the pinned commit (not 25 files); expected: the 3 novel rows and their kind become ordinary output; measure rows per library and minutes",
   "pin every row by (assembly name, signature, IL-body hash) and apply it to any asset whose hash matches; re-validate only rows whose hash changed",
   "witness queue = C-ranked unlabelled candidates that the body proof refused and that are constructible; RabbitMQ.Client / MailKit / StackExchange.Redis first (their used factories are unproved)",
   "consumer run on the census top list (marten, NpgsqlRest, PerformanceMonitor, WebVella-ERP, RepoDB, weasel, wolverine, quartznet, DatabaseManager, aspire ...) with exposure and opportunity counted on the same base (rows beyond production conventions) and the yield bar frozen before any file is fetched"
  ],
  "kill_gate": "0 TRUE findings outside test code over 10 density-selected consumers narrows the whole line to precision and architecture; >1 FALSE among the first 20 reviewed rows kills the breadth step",
